# Model weights never enter git. They are built in the ReboundingPrediction repo
# (`python -m rebounding.cli train` / `train-movement`) and copied in.
#
# The bundles carry their own provenance — build commit, corpus SHA, library versions,
# test scores — so `/healthz` and `rebounding.cli describe` can answer "what is
# deployed?" from the deployed file alone. That is what makes a copy-in workflow safe,
# and it is what was missing when FinalModel.pkl was lost in 2017.
#
# posnn.h5 and msd.pkl were tracked historically; they were removed when the pipeline
# was retrained and nothing loads them any more.
*.pkl
*.h5

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
venv/
rebound-app/venv/
.venv/

# Local publish config for scripts/publish.sh (host, SSH key path) — never commit.
scripts/publish.env

# OS
.DS_Store

# Local pull config for deploy/pg-pull.sh (host, SSH key path) — never commit.
deploy/pg-pull.env
